#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:4
msgid "拡散係数の温度依存性"
msgstr "Temperature Dependence of the Diffusion Coefficient"

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:6
msgid ""
"温度を上げると、Li空孔を含むモデルでLiの拡散係数はどれだけ大きくなるでしょうか。\\ "
"31原子モデルをCHGNetで計算すると、800～1500 Kで拡散係数が増え、拡散の活性化エネルギーは0.43 eVでした。\\ "
"これは文献の長時間NNP-MDの値（0.59 eV）より0.16 eV低く、この温度範囲では拡散係数の温度依存性が文献計算より緩やかです。"
msgstr ""
"How much does the Li diffusion coefficient increase with temperature in a"
" model with a Li vacancy? \\ In the CHGNet calculations for the 31-atom "
"model, the diffusion coefficient increased over 800–1500 K, and the "
"activation energy for diffusion was 0.43 eV. \\ This was 0.16 eV lower "
"than the value of 0.59 eV from long runs with NNP-MD (Li et al.), and the"
" diffusion coefficient varies less strongly with temperature over this "
"range than in their calculations."

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:10
msgid ""
"31原子のLi空孔モデルを、CHGNetによる分子動力学（MD）で4つの温度について計算しました。\\ 各温度の拡散係数 "
":math:`D_{\\mathrm{Li}}` は、 :numref:`{number}. {name} <li3po4-doc-"
"lithium-msd>` で見た平均二乗変位（MSD）の傾きから求めます。"
msgstr ""
"We used CHGNet molecular dynamics (MD) to simulate the 31-atom model with"
" a Li vacancy at four temperatures. \\ At each temperature, we obtain the"
" diffusion coefficient :math:`D_{\\mathrm{Li}}` from the slope of the "
"mean squared displacement (MSD) examined in :numref:`{number}. {name} "
"<li3po4-doc-lithium-msd>`."

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:13
msgid ""
":numref:`li3po4-diffusivity-31atoms` では、横軸に逆温度 "
":math:`1000/T`、縦軸に拡散係数の自然対数を取ります。\\ `アレニウス式 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#arrhenius-equation>`__\\ "
"に従う場合、プロットは直線となり、その傾きの絶対値が大きいほど拡散の活性化エネルギーが高くなります。\\ "
"図の4点を直線で近似すると、活性化エネルギーは0.43 eVとなります。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`li3po4-diffusivity-31atoms` plots the natural logarithm of the "
"diffusion coefficient against inverse temperature :math:`1000/T`. \\ `The"
" Arrhenius equation <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#arrhenius-equation>`__ \\ "
"gives a straight line on this plot when it applies. The greater the "
"absolute value of the slope, the higher the activation energy for "
"diffusion. \\ A straight-line fit to the four points gives an activation "
"energy of 0.43 eV."

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:19
msgid "31原子モデルの4温度の拡散係数の自然対数を逆温度に対して示したグラフ"
msgstr ""
"Plot of the natural logarithm of the diffusion coefficient against "
"inverse temperature for the 31-atom model at four temperatures"

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:24
msgid ""
"31原子モデルのLi拡散係数。点は本計算、黒線はアレニウス式による近似。\\ 図中の文献値「NNP 0.60 eV」「DFT 0.56 "
"eV」は、各手法で求めた移動経路と障壁を使った\\ `速度論的モンテカルロ <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#kinetic-monte-carlo>`__\\ "
"（KMC）の値です。"
msgstr ""
"Li diffusion coefficient in the 31-atom model. The points are from this "
"work, and the black line is a fit to the Arrhenius equation. \\ The "
"published values marked “NNP 0.60 eV” and “DFT 0.56 eV” in the figure "
"come from \\ `kinetic Monte Carlo <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#kinetic-monte-carlo>`__ \\ "
"(KMC) calculations using the migration paths and barriers from the "
"respective methods."

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:27
msgid ""
"文献のKMCの活性化エネルギーは、NNPの経路を使う場合で0.602 eV、DFTの経路を使う場合で0.561 "
"eVです。後者と本計算との差は0.131 eVです。\\ 文献の長時間NNP-"
"MDとKMCでも、同じ小セルで拡散係数の絶対値に差があります。著者らは、KMCで全遷移に共通の\\ `試行頻度 <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#attempt-"
"frequency>`__\\ "
"を設定した近似を一因に挙げています（共通の試行頻度が拡散係数の絶対値に効き、アレニウスプロットの傾きを変えない理由は技術ノートの\\ "
"`熱活性化過程の解釈と限界 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#thermal-activation-"
"limits>`__）。 `Liらの図7とその解説 <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4997242>`__"
msgstr ""
"Li et al. reported a KMC activation energy of 0.602 eV with NNP paths and"
" 0.561 eV with DFT paths. The latter differs from the activation energy "
"in this work by 0.131 eV. \\ For the same small cell, the long NNP-MD "
"runs and KMC in Li et al. also gave different absolute diffusion "
"coefficients. The authors identify their use of a common \\ `attempt "
"frequency <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html"
"#attempt-frequency>`__ \\ for all KMC transitions as one contributing "
"approximation (see \\ `interpretation and limitations of thermally "
"activated processes <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#thermal-activation-limits>`__"
" in the Technical Notes for why a common attempt frequency affects the "
"absolute diffusion coefficient without changing the slope of the "
"Arrhenius plot). `Li et al., Fig. 7 and the accompanying discussion "
"<https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4997242>`__"

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:31
msgid "まとめ"
msgstr "Summary"

#: ../../li3po4/diffusivity-temperature.rst:33
msgid ""
"CHGNetで求めた活性化エネルギー0.43 eVは、文献の長時間NNP-MDの0.59 eVより低くなりました。\\ "
"拡散の活性化エネルギーは、Liが多数回移動したときの拡散係数の温度依存性を表します（1回の移動の障壁との違いは技術ノートの\\ "
"`空孔機構の拡散と活性化エネルギー <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#activation-energy-and-"
"barriers>`__）。\\ 各温度での拡散係数の絶対値を比べるには、構造、ポテンシャル、軌跡長、拡散係数の算出条件を確認します。\\ "
"特に800 Kではホップが少ないと拡散係数が観測時間に敏感になるため、平均二乗変位から傾きが安定して得られるかを確認する必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"The CHGNet activation energy of 0.43 eV was lower than the 0.59 eV from "
"long runs with NNP-MD (Li et al.). \\ The activation energy for diffusion"
" characterizes the temperature dependence of the diffusion coefficient "
"when Li undergoes many hops (see \\ `diffusion via the vacancy mechanism "
"and activation energy <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/md/thermal_activation.html#activation-energy-and-"
"barriers>`__ in the Technical Notes for how it differs from the barrier "
"for a single hop). \\ To compare absolute diffusion coefficients at each "
"temperature, we check the structure, potential, trajectory length, and "
"conditions used to calculate the diffusion coefficient. \\ Particularly "
"at 800 K, the diffusion coefficient is sensitive to the observation time "
"if few hops occur, so we need to check whether the mean squared "
"displacement gives a stable slope."

